---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy — Online Graph Paper Generator';
const description =
  'Privacy policy for onlinegraphpaper.org. The graph paper tools run in your browser, so your drawings and downloads never leave your device.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <span class="kicker">Online Graph Paper Generator</span>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lead">How this site handles your data, in plain language.</p>
      <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> · Privacy Policy</p>
    </section>

    <p>Last updated: 26 October 2026.</p>

    <h2>The Short Version</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Every tool works without an account, and we do not ask for your name or email.</li>
      <li>The graph paper generator runs in your browser, so the grids you draw and the files you download stay on your device.</li>
      <li>We run no advertising and no analytics that identify individual visitors.</li>
      <li>Standard server logs may be kept by our hosting provider and content-delivery network, as described below.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Contents</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><a href="#scope">Who we are &amp; scope</a></li>
      <li><a href="#tool">The tool itself</a></li>
      <li><a href="#collect">Information we collect</a></li>
      <li><a href="#cookies">Cookies &amp; advertising choices</a></li>
      <li><a href="#thirdparty">Third-party services</a></li>
      <li><a href="#legal">Legal bases (GDPR)</a></li>
      <li><a href="#rights">Your rights &amp; choices</a></li>
      <li><a href="#transfers">International data transfers</a></li>
      <li><a href="#retention">Data retention</a></li>
      <li><a href="#children">Children's privacy</a></li>
      <li><a href="#dnt">Do Not Track</a></li>
      <li><a href="#changes">Changes to this policy</a></li>
      <li><a href="#contact">Contact</a></li>
    </ol>

    <h2 id="scope">1. Who We Are &amp; Scope</h2>
    <p>
      This policy applies to onlinegraphpaper.org ("the site", "we", "us"). It covers the pages under
      this domain only. Links to external sites open pages governed by their own privacy policies, and
      we are not responsible for how those sites handle your information.
    </p>

    <h2 id="tool">2. The Tool Itself</h2>
    <p>
      The graph paper generator draws grids and builds PDF, PNG and SVG files in your browser. Nothing
      you draw is sent to our servers, and the files you download are created on your device. You can
      use the whole site without creating an account or providing any personal details.
    </p>

    <h2 id="collect">3. Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>We do not request your name, email address or any other personal information.</p>

    <h3>Usage analytics</h3>
    <p>
      We do not run a third-party analytics service and do not build profiles or behaviour records of
      individual visitors.
    </p>

    <h3>Advertising</h3>
    <p>We do not serve ads and do not set advertising cookies or run ad trackers.</p>

    <h3>Server logs</h3>
    <p>
      Our hosting provider and any content-delivery network may record standard technical data for
      each request — such as IP address, browser type, the page visited and the time — to keep the site
      available and secure. These are routine operational logs, not a record of what you draw.
    </p>

    <h2 id="cookies">4. Cookies &amp; Advertising Choices</h2>
    <p>
      We set no first-party cookies. Because we serve no ads, there are no third-party advertising
      cookies from this site for you to manage.
    </p>

    <h2 id="thirdparty">5. Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>
      The site is delivered by a static hosting provider and, where applicable, a content-delivery
      network. They may keep the server logs described above under their own policies. We do not share
      your drawings or personal details with them, because those never leave your device.
    </p>

    <h2 id="legal">6. Legal Bases (GDPR)</h2>
    <p>
      For visitors in the European Economic Area, the only processing we rely on is our legitimate
      interest in running and securing the site through the minimal server logs described above. We do
      not process personal data for marketing or profiling.
    </p>

    <h2 id="rights">7. Your Rights &amp; Choices</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, restrict or object
      to the processing of your personal data, to receive it in a portable format, and to lodge a
      complaint with a supervisory authority. Because we hold no account data, most requests concern
      the technical logs kept by our hosting provider.
    </p>

    <h2 id="transfers">8. International Data Transfers</h2>
    <p>
      The site may be delivered through servers located in more than one country. Where any technical
      log data is transferred outside the European Economic Area, we rely on recognised safeguards such
      as standard contractual clauses, or the transfer is necessary to deliver the site to you.
    </p>

    <h2 id="retention">9. Data Retention</h2>
    <p>
      We do not store your drawings or any personal information ourselves. Any technical logs are kept
      by our hosting provider only as long as needed for security and operation, then deleted.
    </p>

    <h2 id="children">10. Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The site is a general-audience tool. We do not knowingly collect personal information from
      children under 13. If you believe a child has provided personal information through the site,
      contact us and we will take steps to remove it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="dnt">11. Do Not Track</h2>
    <p>
      Because we do not track visitors across the site, there is nothing for a Do Not Track signal to
      turn off. The site behaves the same whether or not your browser sends that signal.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">12. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time. When we do, we will change the "last updated" date
      at the top of this page.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">13. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For questions about this policy, reach the site owner through the contact details published on
      this website.
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>
